Package: libduckdb1
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: in-process analytical SQL database (shared library)
 DuckDB is an in-process SQL OLAP database management system with a
 vectorised execution engine, columnar storage, MVCC transactions and
 broad support for the SQL standard, including window functions, CTEs
 and complex types (arrays, structs, maps).
 .
 The shared library statically embeds the following in-tree
 extensions, so no additional download is required at runtime:
 autocomplete, core_functions, icu (Unicode collation and timezones),
 json (read_json / JSON functions) and parquet (read_parquet /
 COPY ... TO ... FORMAT PARQUET).
 .
 This package contains the shared library libduckdb.so required at
 runtime by programs that link against DuckDB.

Package: libduckdb-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libduckdb1 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: in-process analytical SQL database (development files)
 DuckDB is an in-process SQL OLAP database management system with a
 vectorised execution engine, columnar storage, MVCC transactions and
 broad support for the SQL standard, including window functions, CTEs
 and complex types (arrays, structs, maps).
 .
 This package contains the C and C++ headers (duckdb.h, duckdb.hpp and
 the duckdb/ tree), the unversioned libduckdb.so symlink, and the
 CMake package config files (DuckDBConfig.cmake, DuckDBConfigVersion.cmake)
 needed to build software against DuckDB.  A worked C-API extension
 example (demo_capi) is shipped under
 /usr/share/doc/libduckdb-dev/examples/.

Package: duckdb
Section: database
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: in-process analytical SQL database (command-line shell)
 DuckDB is an in-process SQL OLAP database management system with a
 vectorised execution engine, columnar storage, MVCC transactions and
 broad support for the SQL standard, including window functions, CTEs
 and complex types (arrays, structs, maps).
 .
 This package contains the duckdb command-line shell, an interactive
 SQL client that can open DuckDB database files and query data in
 CSV, Parquet, JSON and other formats.
